openmediavault-frpc (8.0.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Remove the section dividers from the proxy/visitor form page. The
    Workbench form modifier machinery can only show/hide elements that
    wrap a '.mat-form-field' control; a divider title is not a form
    control, so every conditional section (STCP/XTCP/SUDP, HTTP/HTTPS
    domains, transport options, load balancer, health check, advanced)
    rendered as an empty heading whenever its fields were hidden for the
    selected proxy type. The fields are now laid out flat, like the core
    network interfaces form.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.7) stable; urgency=medium

  * Rework the tagInput fix from 8.0.6 to the official OMV approach: the
    meta, includes, customDomains and locations fields are now stored as
    plain comma-separated strings in the datamodel (like the core ftp
    plugin's tagInput field), instead of arrays bridged in the RPC. The
    8.0.6 bridge was incomplete: OMV's Config.set cannot write a top-level
    string array, so saving those fields always failed.
  * Fix the proxies feature being completely unusable since 8.0.5:
    - Remove "required": true from the proxy 'name' property. OMV's
      ConfigObject::validate() passes a Dictionary object to the JSON
      schema, whose private properties are invisible to get_object_vars(),
      so any field marked required always failed with "Missing 'required'
      attribute 'name'" on every read. Core plugins never mark conf model
      fields required; the UI validator already enforces it.
    - Change the proxied port fields from the union type
      ["integer","string"] to "integer" in the main model. Salt's Python
      datamodel rejects union types, so 'omv-salt deploy run frpc' failed
      to render as soon as a proxy existed.
  * The Workbench 'value' modifier for the proxy role field now sets the
    value via typeConfig (the doModifier() code reads typeConfig, not a
    top-level 'value' key).

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.6) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the WebUI freezing when the FRP Client page is opened. The
    Workbench 'tagInput' control reads its value as a string (it calls
    value.split()), but Frpc.get/getProxy returned the array fields
    (meta, includes, customDomains, locations) as arrays; a non-empty
    array threw "value.split is not a function", the formPage block-ui
    overlay never cleared and the whole SPA navigation got stuck. The
    RPC now bridges these fields to comma-separated strings (set/setProxy
    split them back into arrays for the datamodel and the Salt template),
    and the tagInput defaults in the form YAML are "" instead of [].
  * Fix the proxy form 'role' modifier: a 'value' modifier reads the new
    value from typeConfig, not a top-level 'value' key, so the previous
    form never reset role to 'server'. Use typeConfig: "server".
  * Make the native systemd backend the default: the datamodel default,
    the confdb create.d initial value, the Workbench select (native is
    now the first option), the engined fallbacks and the Salt state all
    default to "native" instead of "docker". Existing configurations
    keep their stored backend; only fresh installs get the new default.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Render the generated systemd unit file as a Jinja template. The
    state did not pass "template: jinja", so the literal
    "{{ pillar['headers']['multiline'] }}" was written as line 1 of
    /etc/systemd/system/frpc.service and systemd logged "Assignment
    outside of section. Ignoring." on every invocation.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Make the generated frpc.toml valid for the bundled frpc 0.71.0:
    - Remove the "Print proxied content" option; it wrote an unsupported
      "printContent" key into [log], so frpc refused to start with
      'json: unknown field "printContent"'.
    - Write the client metadata to [metadatas] instead of the
      unsupported [meta] table.
    - Write transport multiplexing as tcpMux = true instead of the
      unsupported [transport.multiplexer] table.
    - Emit type specific proxy keys only for the proxy types frpc
      accepts them for: secretKey for stcp/xtcp/sudp; subdomain and
      customDomains for http/https/tcpmux; locations, hostHeaderRewrite,
      httpUser and httpPassword for http only.
    - Skip empty entries when rendering "includes" and "meta". OMV
      stores empty array properties as empty XML elements, which were
      rendered as includes = [""].
  * The proxy form shows subdomain and custom domains for tcpmux (frp
    requires at least one of them) and host header rewrite for http only.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Salt state fix: the native backend branch declared the state ID
    "frpc_systemctl_daemon_reload" twice when the service was disabled,
    so "Apply" failed with "found conflicting ID". The systemd unit is
    now created only while the service is enabled, and stopping the
    service is skipped when no unit file exists.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:45:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix configuration read/write failure ("Failed to index key 'user' of
    'user.0'") caused by data model property names that collide with the
    OMV reserved configuration key list ($enums). Rename the settings
    "user" property to "userPrefix" and the proxy "group" property to
    "loadBalancerGroup". Form labels, translations and the generated
    frpc.toml keys (user, loadBalancer.group) are unchanged.

